{{for|the passive skill|Retaliation (passive skill)}}
'''Retaliation''' is a [[gem tag]] associated with skills that become Usable when a certain condition is met, primarily [[block]]ing or taking damage. Retaliation skills can't be used until they become Usable, and have a [[cooldown]] once used. Because of their restrictive nature, Retaliation skills tend to have significantly higher damage stats.

==Mechanics==
While a Retaliation skill is Usable, an icon will appear over your character's head to show that skill can be used. The condition for a Retaliation skill to become Usable is tracked individually for each skill; for example, {{il|Crushing Fist}} and {{il|Eviscerate}} both have a condition that requires blocking. After blocking a single hit, using Crushing Fist will not cause Eviscerate to not become Usable, and vice versa. Copies of the ''same'' skill will share their usability (and cooldown), however. 

"Usable" refers to the period of time when the skill is allowed to be activated. The skill must be both Usable and off [[cooldown]] to use. Skills cannot become usable while on cooldown from their own conditions, but ''can'' become usable while on cooldown through {{c|mod|#% chance when you use a Retaliation Skill for a different Retaliation Skill to become Usable}}. This does not remove an ongoing cooldown. 

Once a Retaliation skill is used, it loses its Usable state. Modifiers which cause Retaliation skills to "remain Usable" (e.g. {{psl|Measured Retaliation}}, [[No Forgiveness]]) will prevent the skill from losing its Usable state and going on cooldown, but will not refresh the Usable duration.

Retaliation skills cannot be [[exert]]ed, or used by [[Proxy|proxies]]. Even when proxies are summoned, e.g. through {{il|General's Cry}} or {{il|The Saviour}}, they will be unable to use their skill.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jdQKjjI2XFY</ref> Most [[trigger]]s cannot be granted to Retaliation skills, though exceptions exist (e.g. {{il|The Eternal Apple}}).

Retaliation skills cannot be supported by {{il|Multistrike}} and will not [[repeat]] with {{psl|Fatal Flourish}} or while affected by an [[Echoing Shrine]].

